  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif&quot;&gt;The proposed development fails to adequately demonstrate that the outbuilding will remain ancillary to the main dwellinghouse, and may instead be considered to operate as a semi-independent accommodation. This would disrupt the established pattern of development in the area and could constitute undue harm to neighbouring occupiers with regards to increased noise and disturbances.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(51, 51, 51);&quot;&gt;As such, the proposed development is contrary to: - National Planning Policy Framework National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (August 2026) - Policies D1, D4, D5, D6 and D14 of the London Plan (March 2021) - Policies DMD1, DMD5, DMSI3 and SP2&amp;nbsp; of&amp;nbsp; The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan 2037 (September 2024) - The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
